# The Incus that CI installs from Zabbly's stable repository (#2733), read by
# .github/scripts/install-incus.sh in every job that installs Incus on a runner.
# Zabbly's stable repository serves a new Incus release to everyone the day it is built, so an
# unpinned install made a new release first show up as a red release run (#2720).
# It lives here, not in a workflow, so the upstream watch can bump it: its app may not change a
# workflow file (docs/dev/UPSTREAM-SETUP.md). The item `zabbly-incus` of upstream/manifest.yaml moves
# it; the version is the one the repository's index lists, that index hashed by the suite's Release
# file, whose signature the engine checks against upstream/keys/zabbly.asc.
# The version is noble's amd64 build, the runners' Ubuntu 24.04. Zabbly keeps only the newest two
# builds, so a pin two releases old no longer installs.
ZABBLY_INCUS_VERSION=1:7.7-ubuntu24.04-202611270613
